                     (193500 x 178600 units)
Window area = 11533600000 square units
Fraction of frame area: 0.334
```


:::
:::


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
plot(fire_month_owin)
```

::: {.cell-output-display}
![](Hands-on_Ex03_files/figure-html/unnamed-chunk-14-1.png){width=672}
:::
:::

### Computing Spatio-temporal KDE

Next, spattemp.density() of sparr package is used to compute the STKDE.


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
st_kde <- spattemp.density(fire_month_owin)
summary(st_kde)
```

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}

```
Spatiotemporal Kernel Density Estimate

Bandwidths
  h = 15102.47 (spatial)
  lambda = 0.0304 (temporal)

No. of observations
  741 

Spatial bound
  Type: polygonal
  2D enclosure: [512066.8, 705559.4] x [9655398, 9834006]

Temporal bound
  [1, 12]

Evaluation
  128 x 128 x 12 trivariate lattice
  Density range: [1.233458e-27, 8.202976e-10]
```


:::
:::

### Plotting the spatio-temporal KDE object

In the code chunk below, plot() of R base is used to the KDE for between July 2023 - December 2023.


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
tims <- c(7,8,9,10,11,12)
par(mfcol=c(2,3), mar=c(3,3,2,1))  # add room for titles with mar()

for(i in tims){
  plot(st_kde, i,
       override.par = FALSE,
       fix.range = TRUE,
       main = "")   # leave main empty
  title(main = paste("KDE at month", i), cex.main = 0.9, line = 1)
}
```

::: {.cell-output-display}
![](Hands-on_Ex03_files/figure-html/unnamed-chunk-16-1.png){width=672}
:::
:::


## Computing STKDE by Day of Year

In this section, We will learn how to computer the STKDE of forest fires by day of year.

###  Creating ppp object

In the code chunk below, DayofYear field is included in the output ppp object.

::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
fire_yday_ppp <- fire_sf %>% 
  select(DayofYear) %>%
  as.ppp()
```
:::


### Including Owin object

Next, code chunk below is used to combine the ppp object and the owin object.


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
fire_yday_owin <- fire_yday_ppp[kbb_owin]
summary(fire_yday_owin)
```

